  <article class="almanac-prose">
    <section id="model" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>02.1 · four inputs</span>
        <h2>Principal. Action. Resource. Context.</h2>
        <p>Every Cedar request has the same grammar. Dekopon supplies each value from authenticated transport state, owner-controlled configuration, and the loaded provider manifest—not from message text or provider input.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cedar-equation" role="group" aria-label="Cedar authorization inputs">
        <div><span>who</span><strong>principal</strong><code>maintainer</code></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">×</i>
        <div><span>does what</span><strong>action</strong><code>gh.pull-request.comment</code></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">×</i>
        <div><span>to which surface</span><strong>resource</strong><code>Provider::"gh"</code></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">+</i>
        <div><span>under which route</span><strong>context</strong><code>via + agent</code></div>
      </div>

      <div class="comparison-table-wrap">
        <table class="almanac-table strategy-table">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Cedar term</th><th scope="col">Dekopon value</th><th scope="col">Trusted source</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Principal</th><td>The human or service asking</td><td>peer identity or subject mapping</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Action</th><td><code>agent.prompt</code> or one capability ID</td><td>fixed action plus loaded manifests</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Resource</th><td>An Agent for prompting; a Provider for capabilities</td><td>route agent or loaded provider</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Context</th><td><code>via</code>, subject, agent, effect, risk, idempotency</td><td>broker-derived identity and trusted classification</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="article-callout callout-decision">
        <strong>A capability is an action, not ambient access.</strong>
        <p>The agent catalog says what a model may propose. Cedar says whether this principal may request that action on this resource. The broker still applies a separate execution envelope before anything runs.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="story" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>02.2 · the running example</span>
        <h2>A PR commenter, not an approver.</h2>
        <p>A maintainer sends a Slack message: “Read PR 42 and leave a concise review comment.” The agent may read the pull request and changed files, then submit a <code>COMMENT</code> review. It has no approval, merge, request-changes, issue, or raw API capability.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="commenter-story">
        <div><small>identity</small><strong>maintainer</strong><span>through <code>chat-gateway</code></span></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
        <div><small>agent</small><strong>pr-commenter</strong><span>three proposed actions</span></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
        <div><small>provider</small><strong>gh</strong><span>GET, then bounded POST</span></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
        <div><small>result</small><strong>COMMENTED</strong><span>identity + policy + digest audited</span></div>
      </div>

      <p>The identifiers below are fictional. Deployment paths and unrelated server limits are omitted. The credential value is visibly redacted. Every permission-bearing relationship remains.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="catalog" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>02.3 · proposal surface</span>
        <h2>The catalog tells the agent what it may ask for.</h2>
      </div>

      <pre><code><span class="code-comment"># dekopon.yaml — public catalog, no secret values</span>
apiVersion: dekopon.dev/v1alpha1
kind: Provider
metadata:
  name: gh
spec:
  description: Narrow GitHub pull-request operations
  type: github
  credentialRef: github-comment-token
status: Unknown
---
apiVersion: dekopon.dev/v1alpha1
kind: Capability
metadata:
  name: gh.pull-request.read
spec:
  description: Reads one pull request
  provider: gh
  effect: read-only
  risk: Low
  idempotency: idempotent
  permissions:
    - operation: pull_requests:read
status: Unknown
---
apiVersion: dekopon.dev/v1alpha1
kind: Capability
metadata:
  name: gh.pull-request.files
spec:
  description: Lists changed files with bounded patches
  provider: gh
  effect: read-only
  risk: Low
  idempotency: idempotent
  permissions:
    - operation: pull_requests:read
      resource: files
status: Unknown
---
apiVersion: dekopon.dev/v1alpha1
kind: Capability
metadata:
  name: gh.pull-request.comment
spec:
  description: Submits a COMMENT review pinned to the observed head SHA
  provider: gh
  effect: external-write
  risk: Medium
  idempotency: conditional
  permissions:
    - operation: pull_requests:write
      resource: reviews
status: Unknown
---
apiVersion: dekopon.dev/v1alpha1
kind: Agent
metadata:
  name: pr-commenter
spec:
  description: Reads pull requests and leaves review comments
  enabled: true
  modelClass: reasoning
  capabilities:
    - gh.pull-request.read
    - gh.pull-request.files
    - gh.pull-request.comment
  providers:
    - gh
status: Ready</code></pre>

      <p>This file narrows the model-facing surface. It grants no provider credential and creates no Cedar permission. Removing a capability stops the model from reaching it through this agent; adding one still requires broker configuration and policy.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="broker" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>02.4 · identity and execution</span>
        <h2>The broker owns everything that carries authority.</h2>
        <p>The same configuration establishes the gateway’s attestor lane and the hard envelope for each capability. The secret value lives in a separate stricter file.</p>
      </div>

      <pre><code><span class="code-comment"># broker.yaml — relevant fields, deployment paths omitted</span>
apiVersion: dekopon.dev/brokerd/v1alpha1
brokerPrincipal: local-broker
policyRevision: pr-commenter-2026-08
policiesPath: policies.cedar
credentialsPath: broker-credentials.yaml
providers:
  - gh-provider.wasm

identities:
  - uid: 65532
    principal: chat-gateway
    actor:
      type: service
      principal: chat-gateway
    attestor:
      namespaces: [slack.t0example]
      chatScopes:
        - breadth: transportWide
          kind: slack
          transport: workspace-slack

identityMappings:
  - subject: slack.t0example.u0example
    principal: maintainer

constraintSets:
  gh.pull-request.read:
    provider: gh
    effect: read-only
    risk: Low
    idempotency: idempotent
    credential: github-comment-token
    constraints:
      timeoutMs: 10000
      maxOutputBytes: 32768
      http:
        allowedHosts: [api.github.com]
        allowedMethods: [GET]
        maxRequests: 1
        maxRequestBytes: 16384
        maxResponseBytes: 262144
        allowPlaintextLoopback: false

  gh.pull-request.files:
    provider: gh
    effect: read-only
    risk: Low
    idempotency: idempotent
    credential: github-comment-token
    constraints:
      timeoutMs: 10000
      maxOutputBytes: 131072
      http:
        allowedHosts: [api.github.com]
        allowedMethods: [GET]
        maxRequests: 1
        maxRequestBytes: 16384
        maxResponseBytes: 1048576
        allowPlaintextLoopback: false

  gh.pull-request.comment:
    provider: gh
    effect: external-write
    risk: Medium
    idempotency: conditional
    credential: github-comment-token
    constraints:
      timeoutMs: 15000
      maxOutputBytes: 8192
      http:
        allowedHosts: [api.github.com]
        allowedMethods: [GET, POST]
        maxRequests: 2
        maxRequestBytes: 16384
        maxResponseBytes: 262144
        allowPlaintextLoopback: false</code></pre>

      <pre><code><span class="code-comment"># broker-credentials.yaml — separate owner-only file</span>
apiVersion: dekopon.dev/broker-credentials/v1alpha1
credentials:
  - name: github-comment-token
    kind: bearerToken
    scheme: Bearer
    destinations: [api.github.com]
    secret: [REDACTED]</code></pre>

      <div class="invariant-notes">
        <article><span>pre-read</span><h3>Why GET and POST?</h3><p>The comment capability reads the pull request first, pins the observed head SHA, then writes the review. A moved head refuses before the write.</p></article>
        <article><span>destination</span><h3>Why repeat the host?</h3><p>The constraint set and credential binding must both cover <code>api.github.com</code>. Startup proves they agree.</p></article>
        <article><span>secret</span><h3>Who sees the value?</h3><p>Only the native broker HTTP engine. It injects the header after guest headers are validated.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="policy" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>02.5 · two independent grants</span>
        <h2>Driving the agent does not imply using its capabilities.</h2>
        <p>The first statement opens the session. The second describes the GitHub surface available inside it. Both require the attested gateway path.</p>
      </div>

      <pre><code><span class="code-comment">// policies.cedar — complete policy set for this example</span>
@id("maintainer-may-prompt-pr-commenter")
permit(
  principal == Dekopon::Principal::"maintainer",
  action == Dekopon::Action::"agent.prompt",
  resource == Dekopon::Agent::"pr-commenter"
)
when {
  context has via &amp;&amp;
  context.via == "chat-gateway"
};

@id("pr-commenter-github-surface")
permit(
  principal == Dekopon::Principal::"maintainer",
  action in [
    Dekopon::Action::"gh.pull-request.read",
    Dekopon::Action::"gh.pull-request.files",
    Dekopon::Action::"gh.pull-request.comment"
  ],
  resource == Dekopon::Provider::"gh"
)
when {
  context has agent &amp;&amp;
  context.agent == "pr-commenter" &amp;&amp;
  context has via &amp;&amp;
  context.via == "chat-gateway"
};</code></pre>

      <p>An empty policy set permits nothing. An unknown principal, provider, action, entity type, or ill-typed expression refuses broker startup under strict validation. The <code>@id</code> values become stable <code>policy_ids</code> in audit.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="decision" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>02.6 · one decision</span>
        <h2>A comment passes through two different gates.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="permission-gates">
        <article>
          <span>Gate A · Cedar</span>
          <h3>May this identity request it?</h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>principal</dt><dd><code>maintainer</code></dd></div>
            <div><dt>action</dt><dd><code>gh.pull-request.comment</code></dd></div>
            <div><dt>resource</dt><dd><code>Provider::"gh"</code></dd></div>
            <div><dt>context</dt><dd><code>pr-commenter</code> via <code>chat-gateway</code></dd></div>
          </dl>
          <strong class="gate-result">Allowed by <code>pr-commenter-github-surface</code></strong>
        </article>
        <i aria-hidden="true">then →</i>
        <article>
          <span>Gate B · constraints</span>
          <h3>How narrowly may it execute?</h3>
          <dl>
            <div><dt>destination</dt><dd><code>api.github.com</code></dd></div>
            <div><dt>methods</dt><dd><code>GET</code> + <code>POST</code></dd></div>
            <div><dt>calls</dt><dd>at most 2</dd></div>
            <div><dt>credential</dt><dd><code>github-comment-token</code></dd></div>
          </dl>
          <strong class="gate-result">Bound to one invocation</strong>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p>The resulting authorization is created and consumed inside the broker. The gateway and model receive the result, never a reusable grant.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="limits" class="article-section">
      <div class="article-heading">
        <span>02.7 · the separation that matters</span>
        <h2>A policy edit cannot move the hard walls.</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="comparison-table-wrap">
        <table class="almanac-table strategy-table">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Cedar may change</th><th scope="col">Cedar cannot change</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>which principal may act</td><td>the destination host or port</td></tr>
            <tr><td>which capability action it may request</td><td>HTTP methods, calls, or byte ceilings</td></tr>
            <tr><td>which provider resource it may target</td><td>timeout, provider output, or host ceilings</td></tr>
            <tr><td>which gateway and agent context must be present</td><td>which broker-held credential is selected</td></tr>
            <tr><td>whether trusted effect/risk/idempotency context matches</td><td>provider input, URL path, headers, or message text</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="article-callout callout-warning">
        <strong>Policy does not currently bind a repository path.</strong>
        <p>Cedar does not receive provider input, so it cannot say “only repositories under this organization.” Use a GitHub token scoped to the intended repositories; credential scope remains that boundary.</p>
      </div>

      {{ docsCta("Open the current Cedar adapter contract", "https://github.com/dekopon-agents/dekopon/blob/main/crates/dekopon-policy/README.md", "See the generated schema, strict validation, context fields, policy bounds, explanations, and digest rules used by the latest code.") }}
    </section>

